    "sodium molybdate (molybdenum)",
    "explicit Fe/Zn/Mn/Co/Cu trace salts",
    "MgCl2·6H2O identity"
   ],
   "corrections": [],
   "notes": "Autotroph: carbon fixed from the carbonate/bicarbonate soda buffer (upregulated RuBisCO), no organic C source. Nitrogen for this (thiocyanate) medium comes from thiocyanate itself, so no NH4Cl is added. Trace solution = DSMZ SL-4 (the 'Pfennig' trace element solution, ref 38); Cu was boosted to 30 µg/L final because Cu is the TcDH cofactor. SL-4 contains NO vitamins, Se, or W, so those are genuinely absent. The auto-generated Calcium (EX_ca2_e) and Fe3+ (EX_fe3_e) entries have no support in the recipe (no Ca salt; only Fe2+ from FeSO4)."
  },
